```markdown
---
name: glossary-cards
description: Format supplied glossary records into flashcard import TSV using only supplied translations. Use when asked to format pasted glossary records; do not use to translate new words or supply missing translations.
---

# Glossary cards

Convert supplied glossary records into tab-separated flashcard import text.

## Read the input

- Identify each source record and its front, back and optional tags fields.
- Number input records from 1 in their original order. Keep these row numbers when reporting omissions.
- If record boundaries or field mappings are ambiguous, ask one focused clarification before formatting.
- Use only the supplied field values. Never invent, translate, correct or enrich a translation from memory or external sources.
- Treat a missing, null, empty or whitespace-only front or back as missing. Omit that record and report its original input row number and missing field(s).
- An absent, null or empty tags field becomes an empty third field. Never infer tags.
- Preserve the supplied values of valid fields, source order and duplicate records. Do not sort or deduplicate.
- If a field contains a literal tab or line break, request a delimiter-safe value before producing the import text; do not silently change its content.

## Return the result

Return the valid records in a fenced `tsv` block. Each data row must contain exactly:

front<TAB>back<TAB>tags

Use literal tab characters, no header and one record per line. An empty tags field still requires the second tab at the end of that row.

If any records were omitted, add a separate note after the TSV block:

Issues:
- Input row N: missing back; omitted.

Name every missing required field for each omitted record. Keep the Issues note outside the TSV so it cannot become an imported card. If no valid records remain, leave the TSV block empty and report the Issues. If there are no issues, omit the note.

A request to translate new words is outside this skill. Ask for supplied translations instead of generating them. A familiar word with a missing back must still be omitted and flagged.

## Check completion

Before replying, confirm that every retained record has three fields, retained records follow source order, absent tags remain empty, and every omitted record appears in Issues with its original row number. Confirm that no translation or tag was invented.

The three authored examples are in [evals/cases.json](evals/cases.json). Their expected TSV strings describe the code-block contents; `issues` describes the separate note.
